  "answer": "Yes",
  "reasoning": "Prioritize the victim’s safety and legal obligations. If a smashed glass cut someone—especially if it appears intentional, caused significant injury, involves a minor, or suggests ongoing abuse—you should report it to emergency services or the police and ensure the injured person receives medical care. If it was a clear, minor accident and everyone agrees no authorities are needed, at minimum provide/seek first aid and document the incident; but when in doubt, report so professionals can assess risk. Laws and duties to report vary by jurisdiction, so err on the side of protecting the injured person."
}

