{
  "answer": "Yes",
  "reasoning": "A shove is physical aggression and can escalate. Prioritizing safety and preventing further harm outweighs personal loyalty. Report to the appropriate authority (security, school administrator, workplace HR, or police if someone is injured or there's immediate danger), and document what you saw (who, when, what happened, witnesses). If you’re worried about safety or retaliation, use anonymous reporting if available and encourage the victim to get medical care or support. You can also tell your friend you reported it and urge them to take responsibility and seek help, but do not cover up violent behavior."
}

